# Build-context filter for Dockerfile (both targets). Two jobs: keep SECRETS + STATE out of the daemon
# (a fat context can leak .env/data into a layer), and keep the context small so `COPY . .` cache-busts
# only on real source changes. NOT ignored on purpose: `patches/` (pnpm patchedDependencies — a frozen
# install refuses to run without them) and `scripts/` (the fleet front door ships in the gpu target).

# secrets + state — the load-bearing exclusions
.env
.env.*
data/
docker/secrets/
docker/*.local.env

# dependency + build output (rebuilt in-image)
node_modules
**/node_modules
packages/client/dist

# the multi-GB engine stores (the main checkout's store root is the repo root)
.cache
.models

# VCS + dev tooling
.git
# …EXCEPT the four plain-text ref files the build stage reads to stamp /app/version.json (the build
# identity every surface reports — docker/assemble-runtime.sh). No objects, no history, no packfiles: HEAD
# plus the loose branch/tag refs plus the packed table. Measured on this repo 2026-09-18: HEAD 21 B,
# packed-refs ~14.4 KiB, refs/heads ~861 B over 21 files, refs/tags 0 — well under 16 KiB total, against a
# .git/objects store three orders of magnitude larger, which stays excluded. Without these the image can
# only report `unknown` for its own commit, which is the exact thing a bug report needs.
!.git/HEAD
!.git/refs/heads/**
!.git/refs/tags/**
!.git/packed-refs
.github
.claude
.devcontainer
.vscode

# tests + docs + reports — never part of the runtime
tests/
docs/
reports/
coverage/
.stryker-tmp
playwright/
test-results/

# misc noise
*.log
.DS_Store
